      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-12-12_WidnesExaminer_art0183" n="art0183">
        <head>NORTH CHESHIRE LEAGUE.</head>
        <p>NORTH CHESHIRE LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>MACKENNALL'S INSTITUTE v. STOCKTON HEATH. _</p>
        <p>The above team; 7u-et. on Saturday on the Institute ground, in the North Cheshire League (Second Division), when the home captain won the toss and elected to start with the slope in his favour. There was a strong wind blowing across the field. From the kick-off the visitors assumed the aggressive, and were soon attack- ing the home goal. Vernon passed out to Lloyd, on the right, and, from his centre, the home defence had to concede a corner. The home team got this away, and play was transferred to the visitors' end, where three corners were forced in quick succession, but no scoring was done. Noden got the ball and passed on to Lloyd, who raced away to the home end, and, from his centre, Vernon passed on to Smith, iwhen the latter was tripped up inside the penalty area. The same player was entrusted with the kick, but shot straight at the goal- keeper, and the ball was got away. Even play in mid-field followed, and when the interval arrived nothing had been scored. On the resumption, Starkey at once raced away on the visitors' left, and, from his centre, the home custodian made a splendid clearance. The home forwards then took play to the oppo- site end, and the visitors' defenders were severely tried and had to concede two corner- kicks, which, however, were not improved upon. Lloyd, by a grand run on the right, again put the home goal in danger and was tripped up just outside the penalty area. Mor- timer took the kick and the ball cannoned off one of the Ow- ~ The home forwards then set up a determined lttack on the visitors' goal, and Smith ileaded a keen drive over the bar. The Institute ecrs''nued to have the best of the play, but the v. :tors' defence was stubborn. Three corners woo conceded, but they yielded no score, and then the visitors' forwards broke away and transferred play to the home end, where Starkey missed scoring when in front of an open goal. Lloyd, Barlow, Chesters, Vernon and Gosling played well for the visitors, and Cowsgill and Skelhorne and the centre-half were the pick of the home team. Result: Macken- nail's Institute, 0; Stockton Heath, 0.</p>
        <p>EMMANUEL INSTITUTE v. PENKETH FRIENDS. On Saturday Emmanuel Institute had a soft job on hand. Their opponents were the Penketh Friends, and they beat them to the tune of 7 goals to nothing.</p>
      </div>
