        <p>ROYAL COURT THEATRE, at 6.50 and 9.0. MONDAY NEXT, AND DURING THE WEEK. (No Performance Tuesday Evening owing to War Meeting in the Theatre.) Mr. W. V. GARROD and his Company, including Miss BERTHA KINGSTON. MONDAY and WEDNESDAY EVENING, and MONDAY MATINEE, at 2.30. "A WIFE FOR A DAY." By W. V. GARROD. THURSDAY, FRIDAY and SATURDAY EVENING, Wilson Barrett's Domestic Drama: "THE SLEDGE HANIMEII." In the last scene occurs the terrible fight with sledge hammers between two blacksmiths. POPULAR PRICES. Telephone 460.</p>
        <p>ROYAL COURT THEATRE, WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY) EVENING, DECEMBER 1311 h, at 8.15. GRAND CONCERT ARTISTIC In aid of the BELGIAN RED CROSS SOCIETY, under distinguished patronage. - BELGIAN STATE ARTISTES will appear, .assisted by: MR. W. V. GARROD, Reciter (the well-known actor), MISS SARA SILCOCK, MISS ELSIE WILKINSON, MRS. E. A. SANDERS. Accompanist: MR. ALBERT TROW. SPECIAL ORCHESTRA. Under the direction of Mr. JAMES ROY. Stalls, 2/6 and 2/-; Grand Circle, 2/- and 1/6; Gallery, 6d.; Pit, 9d.; Promenade, 1/-. Ticket-holders admitted by Special Door.</p>
