        <p>WARRINGTON PARISII CHURCH. A MEMORIAL SERVICE FOR FRANK M. APPLETON, V.D. (Major 4th South Lancashire (Territorial) Bat- talion; Lieut.-Colonel Warrington Battalion Church Lads' Brigade), Who died at the War Station, Tunbridge Wells, on the 6th December, 1914, will be held at the PARISH CEITJRCH, TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), at 10.30 a.m. FREDERIC W. WILLIS, Rector. , James G-. Craik and Edward Isherwood, church- wardens. CHURCH LADS' BRIGADE. 2nd LIVERPOOL CADET BATTALION. The Battalion will attend the Memorial Service for their late Commanding Officer, Lieut.-Colonel F. M. Appleton, V.D., at the Parish Church, To-morrow (Sunday) morning. Fall in at the Town Hall, 9.45 a.m. Dress: Review Order. Old C.L.B. lads, please note! Detachments from kindred Associations will kindly fall in as above. The Band of the Blue Coat School will be in attendance. The " Last Post " will be sounded outside the Church after service. JNO. A. BR,OOKES. Major. Officer Commanding.</p>
