        <p>DEATH OF YiAJOR AppLEToN, V.D.</p>
        <p>Warrington wag startled late on Sunday by the news that Major Appleton had been found shot through the head in Tunbridge Wells, at which place the Warrington Territorials, in which he was the senior major, are at present stationed. Major Appleton was regarded with affection by the whole of the past and present members of the Battalion, and was held in the sincerest respect by Warringtonians generally, who found in him a patriot and a gentleman of un- failing courtesy. To both the Territorials and the town his loss will be a severe blow, while the country, at the present juncture, can ill afford to lose the ser-</p>
