        <p>LEAGUE LEADERS' OPE GOAL WIN • Free-kick Gives Them Victory Over Hollins Green. • • KEEN GAMES IN A HALF-GALE. Notes by "Linesman." • On Saturday very boisterous weather pre- the centre kick tbe visitors tried hard to fight vailed throughout this district, but, in spite of their way through, but were not able to make the unsatisfactory conditions, the usual number much impression on the home defence, Tithers of matches in the local League were brought to and Lawrance holding the forwards in check. satisfactory conclusions. Play was transferred to the opposite end, and after several strong attempts to increase their lead, Gleaves succeeded in scoring a second goal. From that point until the interval play was con- fined to the visitors' end, but Millar, Pilling and Evans defended very well and the home for- wards could not get through again. The score at half-time was 2-0 in favour of the home team. On resumption the visitors had the assistance of the wind, and forced several corner kicks, from one of which they scored their first goal. The ball was well placed by Gifford, and Dag- nall, in attempting the clearance, had the mis- fortune to put it through his own goal. The equalising goal came directly after from a splen- did shot by Stubbs, taken at a range of thirty yards from goal. A shot from Gifford was headed over the bar by Tithers. The home for- wards broke away and Gleave sent across a grand centre, but it was allowed to pass un- accepted, and about half a minute before time expired Meachin shot wide when in a good posi- tion. Result: Newton Cons., 2 goals; Orford , White Star, 2 goals.</p>
